@startuml
skinparam {
    ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    BoundaryBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ControlBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    EntityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

    ActorBorderColor black
    BoundaryBorderColor black
    ControlBorderColor black
    EntityBorderColor black
    DatabaseBorderColor black
}

actor User
boundary "Reading History Page (UI)" as UI
boundary Router
control ChapterController
control ChapterService
entity HistoryModel
database MongoDB

User -> UI: 1. Click delete story history
activate User
activate UI

UI -> Router: 2. DELETE /history/{userId}/{storyId}
activate Router

Router -> ChapterController: 3. deleteStoryHistory()
activate ChapterController

ChapterController -> ChapterController: 4. Parse params & convert ObjectId
activate ChapterController
ChapterController -> ChapterService: 5. deleteStoryHistory(userId, storyId)
deactivate ChapterController

activate ChapterService
ChapterService -> HistoryModel: 6. deleteOne({user_id, story_id})
activate HistoryModel

HistoryModel -> MongoDB: 7. Delete history record
activate MongoDB
MongoDB --> HistoryModel: 8. Delete result (deletedCount)
deactivate MongoDB

HistoryModel --> ChapterService: 9. Deletion result
deactivate HistoryModel

opt No history found
    ChapterService --> ChapterController: 9.1. Return message: No history found
    ChapterController --> Router: 9.2. HTTP response
    Router --> UI: 9.3. Show result message
    UI --> User: 9.4. Display notification
end

ChapterService --> ChapterController: 10. Return message: History deleted successfully
deactivate ChapterService

ChapterController --> Router: 11. HTTP response
deactivate ChapterController
Router --> UI: 12. Show result message
deactivate Router
UI --> User: 13. Display notification
deactivate UI
deactivate User
@enduml
